Option 1: STM32 HAL + Custom S‑Curve (Recommended)

This is a complete, non‑blocking example using STM32Cube HAL. It generates a PWM signal for a standard hobby servo (50 Hz, 0.5 ms–2.5 ms pulse) and glides between angles using a smootherstep S‑curve (zero acceleration at start and end).

Hardware assumptions

STM32 (e.g., Nucleo‑64, Blue Pill, etc.)
Servo signal pin → PA1 (change to your timer channel)
Timer PWM at 50 Hz (20 ms period)
Pulse width: 0.5 ms = 0°, 2.5 ms = 180°
