Practical STM32 Tips

PWM frequency: Standard servos expect 50 Hz (20 ms period). Some digital servos work at 300–500 Hz—check the datasheet; higher refresh can reduce jitter.
Timer tick resolution: If SystemCoreClock = 72 MHz and prescaler = 71 → 1 MHz timer. Period = 20000 ticks = 20 ms. Pulse of 1500 ticks = 1.5 ms = 90°.
Non-blocking: Never use HAL_Delay() inside your movement logic if you need to read sensors simultaneously. Use HAL_GetTick() and a state machine like the example above.
Power: Do not power servos from the STM32 3.3V/5V rail. Use an external 5V–6V supply and common ground. A 100 µF–470 µF capacitor across the servo supply rails helps prevent brownouts.
Jitter: If the servo shakes at the end of a move, add a small deadband (e.g., don’t update if |target - current| < 0.5°) or increase moveDuration.
